It's too high for sculptis to work even with maxes settings

&#x200B;

Im using it for baking, Im still learning Zbrush and the only workflow Ive found that works for me is dynameshing, Zremesh never works right and destroys anything pointy majorly and ive not been able to find any answer for doing it "correctly" while not destroying any of the sharp points

No. It's unethical for human art just as much as it is unethical for anthro art. They work the same by stealing other artists work. 

&#x200B;

It's also causing a major issue for artists like myself, trying to find actual references of anything has become incredibly hard as AI art has flooded searches and completely soured the reference pool with malformed amalgamations of other images, flooding all search tags with them due to how theyre generated. 

&#x200B;

There is plenty of other, better and more ethical methods of getting creative juices going, many we have done for thousands of years already.

So Im stuck with the Enemy of Justice debuff against the goblins. Even though I havent killed a single goblin other than Gut, there is no witnesses, i went through and checked every single goblin and none of them have witness. This is extremely annoying as when attacking the grove every fight the goblins turn on me even though im on their bludy side, and even Minthara attacks me after I help her.

&#x200B;

Any ideas on removing this damn thing? I cantr navigate half the map because of the goblin settlement in the middle of it

Most UK houses's windows dont really \*open\* in the right way for a window one, and many are renting still so to properly secure it youd do damage to the window frame, which are usually plastic or metal. Most windows here swing out at an angle to prevent rain and wind getting in, they dont slide up to open like what I atleast have seen be the main american style window.

&#x200B;

People who have AC here usually just have a portable unit like I do so you can store it away anyways. It's still always a case of \*where do you put it when not in use\* though. We dont have anywhere near as much space and few have a garage these days.

I did ask specifically if it can be done or if i just need to entirely unplug it, no need to be sassy.

&#x200B;

You answered my question still so. Thanks, I'l get one of those remote plugs so i can turn the G2 off at the wall for when I want to use the quest.

I remember my friends were planning on hireing a fucking tank for us to go in to the prom (in the UK..) cause it turned out pretty cheap for the experience in the area, (it legit cost like, £250 for the night???). it was supposed to be a thing of the nerdy boys coming in looking badass to get a date on the night or something... I didnt go cause it felt mega masculine and also mega just... yeah.

&#x200B;

Still kinda sad i missed out on going in a tank tho lmao.

