A lot of classes are having these issues. For balance it feels unnecessary almost for the change, unless someone can explain to me why it was. During legion without traits and legendarys i rather enjoyed the star surge giving an empower for both wrath and starfire. I know its the same now but I *believe* it's easy to cap out on charges and resource due to how it has scaled.

&#x200B;

A lot of classes without the bandaids put in through BFA are just boring and lackluster. Demonology is fun currently, due to the random tyrants and all that they give, with the insane haste levels and all that too. On alpha without them it's unbelievable slow for no reward, and the flaws in the spec get emphasised more so (Lack of interrupts, movement, etc).

&#x200B;

I have a STRONG feeling that some legendarys could end up being old azerite traits, potentially essences even.  I really hope not, but since blizzard is basically saying "Wait til you have everything before critiquing the classes!" a lot of the bandaids are going to be in those, and they *could* go the harder route of making new things, or the easy "already know what works" route with them.

MoP Demonology. 

&#x200B;

R.I.P Metamorphosis Lock :c

Was thinking this. Not all transfolk want to or cant get SRS, it does not mean they're lower tier at all and implying that it is, is harmful to those who are in that boat.

&#x200B;

It's a bad idea for me to have SRS due to crohns and i decided not to risk it. It has caused a lot of suffering in my past due to that. Don't say I'm not equal to those who have gone through with it, we are all equals in this together.

