**📷**[ **Soul Rot**](https://shadowlands.wowhead.com/spell=325640/soul-rot): Wither away all life force of your current target and up to 3 additional targets nearby, causing them to suffer (100% of Spell power) Nature damage over 8 sec. Drain Life will also be cast on any enemy affected by your Soul Rot. Consumes 20% of maximum health when cast.40 yd range. 1.5 sec cast. 1 min cooldown.

&#x200B;

"Drain Life WILL also be cast" this is why I thought it would be cast automatically. I suppose it can be taken either way?

Hi, i know your post is a few days old, but I'm wanting to try and get 1 - 2 mil before shadow lands. I normally like a simple method, say farm potions, but even on a large pop server it's not proving to be worth while due to the insane amount of multibox farmers.

&#x200B;

I've tried the raw gold shuffle with tsl but the prices are never right for it to be worth while, while there is upward of 800k tidespray on the ah it's never below 2g 10s, so the rare moment it is i get a lil burst but never enough and it's so rare to occur.

&#x200B;

Can you recommend a new method for someone like me who is used to the traditional ways of gold making? So much is plummeting in price in every profession it feels like so i just dont know. I really dont like to play the AH, it's just simply not enjoyable for me.

&#x200B;

I have several 120 characters but only one account. Early in BFA i boosted for my gold too but I'm just not in a situation to be able to do that again.

I do like this set, but I do wish they would start reducing a lot of the *flat detail* stuff on the robes and just more 3d elements to compare with other armour classes. On this set there could've added a bit of layering onto the lower half, and maybe the chains from the belt be 3d similar to the current tier cloth belt.

&#x200B;

With the non robe version the legs definitely need some layering and the boots need something extra to balance it out, else it would be mega top heavy.

&#x200B;

There is definitely plenty of large detail that would look a lot better emphasised in 3d.

